BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Eating Healthy on a Budget
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260523T150000
UID:69e51e035c04bc0fc062d56b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:With the cost of food rising\, we'll look at ways families can
  save on their grocery bill. We'll cover tips for meal planning at home wi
 th children\, as well as\, how to maximize grocery shopping while shopping
  at the store including the “best buys” in various foods. In this work
 shop\, we will cover general tips to help stretch every food dollar\, as w
 ell as tips to manage food waste\, especially when feeding a family.\nPres
 ented in partnership with\nToronto Public Health
LOCATION:McGregor Park\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e51e035c04bc0fc062d56b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
